@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nii-il04-nouns`

-- National Insurance Law [Consolidated Version], s 1 (הגדרות) — ONLY the definitions that ss 334
-- and 337 and Schedule J use. Every other term s 1 defines is listed, with the reason it is not
-- encoded here, in NOTES.md's coverage table.
-- Quotations (`src:N`) are copied mechanically from line N of
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/national-insurance-law-consolidated-version-5755-1995.he.wiki.txt.

§ `Section 1 — definitions`
-- src:120 | סעיף 1 – הגדרות [תיקון: תשנ״ז־5, תש״ס־4, תשס״ג־5, תשס״ג־8, תשס״ג־11, תשס״ד, תשס״ה־2, תשס״ו־8, תשס״ט־3, תש״ע־9, תשע״ב־14, תשע״ג־3, תשע״ד־6, תשע״ד־12, תשע״ו־3, תשע״ו־8, תשע״ז־5, תשע״ז־12, תשע״ז־16, תשע״ז־19, תשע״ח־4, תשע״ח־5, תשפ״ב־3, תשפ״ג־8, תשפ״ד־12, תשפ״ה־3, תשפ״ה־11, תשפ״ו, תשפ״ו־7]
-- src:121 | בחוק זה –

§§ `"the Minister"`

-- s 337(b) gives the power to change the rates in Schedule J to "the Minister". The definition is
-- a pure carrier of words: nothing computes with it, and the order record's `made by the
-- Minister` field means this office. (The Law's front matter lists later notices changing
-- ministerial titles; they are not in this row.)
-- src:126 | ”השר“ – שר העבודה והרווחה;
@ref National Insurance Law s 1, "השר" (source line 126)
GIVETH A STRING
`s 1 — "the Minister"` MEANS "the Minister of Labour and Welfare"

§§ `"the index"`

-- s 334(a)(1) updates the reduced collection threshold "by the rate of rise of the index". The
-- index is the consumer price index the Central Bureau of Statistics publishes each month: a
-- published figure, so every index reading in this row is an input (nii-s334-interpretation.l4).
-- src:171 | ”מדד“ – מדד המחירים לצרכן שמפרסמת מדי חודש הלשכה המרכזית לסטטיסטיקה;

§§ `"employer" and "employee"`

-- src:172 | ”מעביד“, ”מעסיק“ – מי שמעסיק אדם במסגרת יחסי עבודה;
-- src:204 | ”עובד“ – לרבות בן משפחה, אף אם אין בינו לבין קרובו המעסיקו יחסי עבודה, ובלבד שהוא עובד במפעל באופן סדיר ובעבודה שאילולא עשה אותה הוא, היתה נעשית בידי עובד; לענין זה, ”בן משפחה“ – אחד ההורים, ילד, נכד, אח או אחות;
-- "employee" INCLUDES ("לרבות") a family member on conditions; its core is the ordinary meaning,
-- a person employed within an employment relationship, which is also how s 1 defines the other
-- side of it, "employer". So the definition is the core OR the family-member limb.
@ref National Insurance Law s 1, "עובד" (source line 204), with "מעביד" (source line 172)
GIVEN p IS A `A person who works`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1 — the person is an employee` p MEANS
        p's `employed within an employment relationship`
    OR  `s 1 — the family-member limb of "employee"` p

-- "a family member, even though there is no employment relationship between him and his relative
-- who employs him, provided that he works in the enterprise regularly and in work which, had he
-- not done it, would have been done by an employee; for this purpose 'family member' – a parent,
-- a child, a grandchild, a brother or a sister". The three conditions are conjoined.
@ref National Insurance Law s 1, "עובד", the family-member limb (source line 204)
GIVEN p IS A `A person who works`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1 — the family-member limb of "employee"` p MEANS
        p's `a parent, child, grandchild, brother or sister of the relative employing them`
    AND p's `works in the enterprise regularly`
    AND p's `in work which, had they not done it, would have been done by an employee`

-- NOT DECIDED HERE (NOTES.md, fork F11): "employer" requires an employment relationship, and the
-- family-member limb of "employee" expressly has none, so whether the relative is "the employer"
-- of such an employee is not settled by these two definitions. No rule in this row turns on it.

§§ `"self-employed person"`

-- src:206 | ”עובד עצמאי“, לענין שנת מס פלונית או חלק ממנה – מי שעסק באותה תקופה במשלח ידו שלא כעובד (להלן – משלח יד), והתקיים בו אחד מאלה:
-- src:207 | (1) הוא עסק במשלח ידו, לפחות עשרים שעות בשבוע בממוצע;
-- src:208 | (2) הכנסתו החודשית הממוצעת ממשלח ידו לא פחתה מסכום השווה ל־50% מהשכר הממוצע;
-- src:209 | (3) הוא עסק במשלח ידו לפחות שתים עשרה שעות בשבוע בממוצע והכנסתו החודשית הממוצעת ממשלח ידו לא פחתה מסכום כאמור בלוח א׳;
-- src:210 | לענין הגדרה זו רשאי השר לקבוע שיטת חישוב של ממוצעים וכן שיעור אחר במקום השיעור הקבוע בלוח א׳;
-- src:211 | [note: פורסמו תקנות הביטוח הלאומי (חישוב הממוצע של שעות עבודה והכנסה של עובד עצמאי), התשמ״ה–1985.]
-- "for a tax year or part of one – a person who in that period engaged in his occupation not as an
-- employee, and ONE of the following held". The three limbs are a disjunction; the occupation
-- condition is conjoined with it. "at least" and "not less than" are inclusive (AT LEAST).
--
-- `the average wage` is an argument because it is a published figure that moves (s 1 "the
-- average wage", below; NOTES.md fork F5 on which published series to supply). `the sum in
-- Schedule A` is an argument because Schedule A ("15% of the average wage as at the first day of
-- the quarter", source line 4365) is not in this row; and s 1 lets the Minister fix a different
-- rate in its place (source line 210), so the sum is whatever the instruments in force make it.
@ref National Insurance Law s 1, "עובד עצמאי", limb (1) (source line 207)
GIVEN o IS A `A person's occupation in a period`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1 "self-employed person" (1) — at least twenty hours a week on average` o MEANS
    o's `average hours a week in the occupation` AT LEAST 20

@ref National Insurance Law s 1, "עובד עצמאי", limb (2) (source line 208)
GIVEN o                  IS A `A person's occupation in a period`
      `the average wage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1 "self-employed person" (2) — average monthly income of` o `not less than 50% of the average wage of` `the average wage` MEANS
    o's `average monthly income from the occupation` AT LEAST (50% TIMES `the average wage`)

@ref National Insurance Law s 1, "עובד עצמאי", limb (3) (source line 209)
GIVEN o                     IS A `A person's occupation in a period`
      `the sum in Schedule A` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1 "self-employed person" (3) — at least twelve hours a week, and average monthly income of` o `not less than the Schedule A sum of` `the sum in Schedule A` MEANS
        o's `average hours a week in the occupation` AT LEAST 12
    AND o's `average monthly income from the occupation` AT LEAST `the sum in Schedule A`

@ref National Insurance Law s 1, "עובד עצמאי" (source lines 206-211)
GIVEN o                       IS A `A person's occupation in a period`
      `the average wage`      IS A NUMBER
      `the sum in Schedule A` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1 — a self-employed person in the period:` o `with the average wage at` `the average wage` `and the Schedule A sum at` `the sum in Schedule A` MEANS
        o's `engaged in the period in an occupation not as an employee`
    AND (   `s 1 "self-employed person" (1) — at least twenty hours a week on average` o
         OR `s 1 "self-employed person" (2) — average monthly income of` o `not less than 50% of the average wage of` `the average wage`
         OR `s 1 "self-employed person" (3) — at least twelve hours a week, and average monthly income of` o `not less than the Schedule A sum of` `the sum in Schedule A`)

§§ `"the average wage", with "compensation", "the compensation rate" and "update day"`

-- src:212 | ”פיצוי“ – תשלום של תוספת יוקר המשתלמת לפי המדד, תשלום של מקדמה על חשבון תוספת יוקר או תשלום פיצוי בעד התייקרות לעובדים השכירים במשק לפי הסדר בין ארגון העובדים המייצג את המספר הגדול ביותר של העובדים במדינה לבין ארגון מעבידים שלדעת השר הינו ארגון יציג ונוגע בדבר;
-- src:220 | ”שיעור הפיצוי“ – השיעור השווה לשיעור הגדלת שכר העבודה לעובדים השכירים במשק כתוצאה מתשלום הפיצוי;
-- src:222 | ”השכר הממוצע“ – הצירוף של שניים אלה:
-- src:223 | (1) הממוצע החודשי של השכר הממוצע למשרת שכיר בשלושת החודשים האחרונים שלגביהם היו נתונים בידי הלשכה המרכזית לסטטיסטיקה ביום שקדם ליום העדכון (להלן בהגדרה זו – ממוצע השכר);
-- src:224 | (2) תוספת לממוצע השכר בשיעור הפיצוי שניתן בתקופה שמתום שלושת החודשים ששימשו בסיס לחישוב ממוצע השכר ועד ליום העדכון;
-- src:225 | לענין הגדרה זו, ”יום העדכון“ – 1 בינואר של כל שנת מס, ואם חל פיצוי לאחר מכן – 1 בחודש שבו חל הפיצוי; על כל שינוי בשכר הממוצע יפרסם השר הודעה ברשומות;
-- src:226 | [note: השכר הממוצע לפי הגדרה זאת: בשנת 2026, 13,566 ש״ח.]
-- "the COMBINATION of these two: (1) the monthly average of the average wage per employee post in
-- the last three months for which the CBS had data on the day before the update day ('the wage
-- average'); (2) an addition to the wage average at the compensation rate given in the period from
-- the end of those three months to the update day."
-- "The combination" is read as the sum: the wage average plus the addition. Nothing here rounds;
-- the figure the Institute publishes is in whole shekels (nii-il04-published-figures.l4).
-- s 2 (source lines 230-239), not in this row, changes how the average wage is calculated "for
-- benefits and contributions" (exceptional pay months); this rule is s 1 alone (NOTES.md, F5).
@ref National Insurance Law s 1, "השכר הממוצע" (1) (source line 223)
GIVEN d IS A `The data for an update of the average wage`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 1 "the average wage" (1) — the wage average, from` d MEANS
    (     d's `CBS average wage per employee post, first of the three months`
     PLUS d's `CBS average wage per employee post, second of the three months`
     PLUS d's `CBS average wage per employee post, third of the three months`)
    DIVIDED BY 3

@ref National Insurance Law s 1, "השכר הממוצע" (2), with "שיעור הפיצוי" (source lines 224, 220)
GIVEN d IS A `The data for an update of the average wage`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 1 "the average wage" (2) — the addition at the compensation rate, from` d MEANS
    `s 1 "the average wage" (1) — the wage average, from` d
        TIMES d's `compensation rate given from the end of those three months to the update day`

@ref National Insurance Law s 1, "השכר הממוצע" (source lines 222-224)
GIVEN d IS A `The data for an update of the average wage`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 1 — the average wage on an update day, from` d MEANS
         `s 1 "the average wage" (1) — the wage average, from` d
    PLUS `s 1 "the average wage" (2) — the addition at the compensation rate, from` d

-- "'update day' – 1 January of every tax year, and if compensation applies after that – the 1st of
-- the month in which the compensation applies". The months in which compensation applied in the
-- year are an input (a fact the Minister's notices in Reshumot record).
@ref National Insurance Law s 1, "השכר הממוצע", "יום העדכון" (source line 225)
GIVEN `the tax year`                          IS A NUMBER
      `the months in which compensation applies` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`s 1 — the update days of the average wage in tax year` `the tax year` `with compensation applying in months` `the months in which compensation applies` MEANS
    YMD `the tax year` 1 1 FOLLOWED BY map `the first of the month` `the months in which compensation applies`
    WHERE
        `the first of the month` m MEANS YMD `the tax year` m 1

§§ `"tax year"`

-- "as in the Income Tax Ordinance". The Ordinance makes a tax year twelve months from 1 January,
-- or a special assessment period where one is set; this row takes a tax year to be a calendar
-- year and does not model special assessment periods (NOTES.md, F12). It is used only inside
-- "self-employed person" (an input period) and "update day" (above).
-- src:227 | ”שנת מס“ – כמשמעותה בפקודת מס הכנסה;
